in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/math/bundle
in @epistemologic/math/music

# @epistemologic/math/music/harmonic — frequency ratios as the
# number-theoretic substrate of pitch; Pythagorean comma as holonomy.
#
# The audible-register foundation. The smallest sub-shard that proves
# the recognition from `@epistemologic/math/music`'s header at
# substrate altitude: music IS the audible register of (A, H, D), not
# a metaphor laid alongside it.
#
# === The bridge ===
#
# `bundle.mirror` declares: "Holonomy IS loss. Comprehension always
# costs something. Transport returns imperfect by design." That
# sentence is the substrate's deepest claim about why error exists at
# all: a closed loop carried around the principal G-bundle does not
# return to where it started, and the residual IS the loss kintsugi
# reduces tick by tick.
#
# Pythagoras observed the same fact 2500 years earlier in audible
# vocabulary. Twelve perfect fifths (3:2) stacked do NOT close to seven
# octaves (2:1). The residual:
#
#   3^12 / 2^19 = 531441 / 524288 ≈ 1.013643
#
# The Pythagorean comma. The first holonomy ever measured, at the
# audible register, two and a half millennia before the principal
# bundle had a name. The musical scale's entire history of temperaments
# (Pythagorean, meantone, well-tempered, equal-tempered) is a record of
# civilization redistributing this single holonomy across the twelve
# intervals to make the loop close enough for music to be performable.
#
# Equal temperament IS the substrate's name for the kintsugi step that
# smears 23.46 cents of comma uniformly across twelve fifths so each
# one carries 1.955 cents of holonomy instead of one of them carrying
# all of it.
#
# `comma_as_holonomy` IS the bridge action. Once it is substrate-
# declared, the audible register IS substrate-fact: loss has frequency;
# mirror has been computing in audible vocabulary since the bundle
# tower landed.
#
# === Eigenvalue framing (spectral-triple connection) ===
#
# `spectral-triple.mirror` names mirror's H as "5-dim vector spaces
# with the structure group O(5)"; eigenvalues of D are roots of a
# degree-5 characteristic polynomial. The substrate's spectrum has
# five eigenvalues; the audible register reads each one as a
# frequency.
#
# Small-integer ratios on the harmonic series are the consonances the
# spectrum tends toward when kintsugi reduces holonomy:
#
#   1:1  unison      (λ₀ — the autopoietic closure; Lawvere fixed pt)
#   2:1  octave      (the doubling; the next-altitude version of self)
#   3:2  fifth       (the eigenvector pointing toward closure)
#   4:3  fourth      (the inverse of the fifth in the octave's quotient)
#   5:4  major third (the next harmonic; the consonance frontier)
#   6:5  minor third (the conjugate; the chromatic alternative)
#   9:8  whole tone  (the difference of two fifths, octave-reduced; the
#                     load-bearing dissonance — the smallest interval
#                     the scale tolerates as a step)
#
# These ratios ARE the eigenvalues of a 5-dim O(5)-bundle's connection
# operator in the consonant basis — small-integer rationals whose
# spectrum minimises the Hilbert-space residual (per dissonance.mirror,
# when it lands).
#
# === Floor types: substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `boot/std/number.mirror`, `u32` is a kernel primitive. Per
# `shards/glass.mirror`, `ref` is the floor for substrate references.
# For ratios the substrate-pull-correct choice is `u32` for the
# numerator and denominator (small-integer rationals; the discipline
# IS that ratios stay in u32 — when they grow beyond u32 they are no
# longer harmonic).
#
# `cents` is a logarithmic interval measurement: 1200 cents per
# octave; one cent ≈ 1/100 of a semitone in 12-TET. The standard
# psychoacoustic resolution: trained listeners hear about 5 cents.
# Returns `ref` — the float-valued reading lifts through the same
# substrate floor that carries `f64` weights in opacity_map (per
# `glass.mirror`).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Every type and action below names an established music-theoretic
# object older than the discipline of computer science:
#
#   ratio          Pythagoras (~530 BCE), Aristoxenus (~330 BCE).
#   pythagorean_comma  Pythagoras (the ratio) → named ~17th-century
#                  music theory; measured by Mersenne (1636).
#   cents          Ellis (1885), `Inaudible Octaves'.
#   consonance     Pythagoras → Helmholtz (1863).
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* these so the eigenboard
# can reason about them. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §5.1 (the sub-shard
#               proposal; the audible-register recognition).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (the
#                      audible register of (A, H, D)),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (numerator and
#                      denominator are u32, the ratio is its own
#                      newtype, the comma is its own newtype).
# Related shards: epistemologic/math/music.mirror (the family root;
#                 the parent altitude),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/bundle.mirror (the
#                 holonomy carrier this shard bridges into the
#                 audible register),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/spectral-triple.mirror
#                 (the 5-dim O(5) eigenvalue framing this shard sees
#                 as harmonic-ratio spectrum),
#                 glass.mirror (verdict; ref; the substrate floor),
#                 boot/std/number.mirror (u32 kernel primitive).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/math/music/harmonic.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/math/music/harmonic` as a species under the
# `@epistemologic/math/music` family.

# === The harmonic-ratio carrier ===
#
# A frequency ratio between two pitches. Numerator and denominator are
# `u32` per the substrate-pull discipline: harmonic ratios are
# small-integer rationals. When a ratio's terms grow beyond u32 it
# has left the harmonic regime — by construction. The discipline IS
# the type.
#
# Normal form: the ratio is in lowest terms (gcd(numerator,
# denominator) = 1). The substrate altitude declares the carrier;
# normalisation is the obligation of the realisation layer.
#
# Identity contract: two ratios are equal iff their normal forms are
# byte-equal. The realisation layer enforces this; the substrate
# names it.
type ratio = {
  numerator:   u32,
  denominator: u32,
}

# === The Pythagorean comma — holonomy at the audible altitude ===
#
# The residual when twelve perfect fifths (3:2)^12 are compared to
# seven octaves (2:1)^7:
#
#   3^12 / 2^19 = 531441 / 524288 ≈ 1.013643
#
# This residual IS holonomy in the audible register. It is the
# substrate's first measured loss — the loop does not close; the
# residual IS the cost of comprehension carried around twelve fifths.
#
# The record carries:
#   excess  — the ratio that fails to be 1:1; the closure residual.
#   cycles  — how many fifth-stacks were traversed (canonically 12).
#
# `cycles` is parametric because the same holonomy structure shows
# up at other cycle counts (the syntonic comma at a different cycle;
# the schisma at a different combination). Naming `cycles` keeps the
# carrier reusable for the comma family without inventing new types.
type pythagorean_comma = {
  excess: ratio,
  cycles: u32,
}

# === Bridge action: comma IS holonomy ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION of this shard.
#
# Lifts a Pythagorean comma into a `holonomy` value of the principal
# G-bundle (per `bundle.mirror`'s `type holonomy` carrier). After this
# action is substrate-declared, the audible register IS substrate-fact:
#
#   - `bundle.mirror` says: "Holonomy IS loss."
#   - This action says:    "A comma IS a holonomy."
#   - Therefore:           "A comma IS loss"
#                          (and: "loss has frequency";
#                           and:  "the substrate has been computing in
#                           audible vocabulary since the bundle tower
#                           landed").
#
# The signature is the bridge. The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`):
# the realisation lifts cents through the holonomy carrier's concrete
# shape, which is itself an abstract type at the bundle altitude (per
# `bundle.mirror` line `type holonomy`). The lift is constrained by
# the type system; the arithmetic lands when a consumer pulls.
comma_as_holonomy(c: pythagorean_comma) -> holonomy { \ }

# === Basic operations on ratios ===
#
# Each operation has a precise meaning at the audible altitude AND
# at the spectral-triple altitude. The substrate declares the
# signatures; the obligation-blocked bodies land when consumers pull.

# compose — interval composition; ratio multiplication.
#
# Audibly: stacking two intervals produces the interval whose ratio
# is the product of their ratios. A fifth (3:2) above a fifth (3:2)
# is a ninth ((3:2)*(3:2) = 9:4 = octave + whole tone).
#
# Spectrally: `compose` IS the algebra operation on the consonant
# basis of H (the 5-dim O(5)-bundle's connection eigenbasis). Per
# `spectral-triple.mirror`'s `compose_a` for the algebra A; the
# harmonic-altitude specialisation of the same morphism.
#
# Normal form: the result is normalised (lowest terms) per the
# `ratio` carrier's identity contract.
compose(a: ratio, b: ratio) -> ratio { \ }

# inverse — interval inversion; numerator/denominator swap.
#
# Audibly: the descending interval of equal magnitude. The inverse
# of a perfect fifth (3:2) is the perfect fourth descended (2:3),
# which octave-equivalences to (4:3) — the perfect fourth ascended.
#
# Spectrally: `inverse` IS the involution on the algebra A — the
# adjoint of `compose`. Required for A to be involutive (per
# `spectral-triple.mirror`'s reference to "an involutive algebra A
# acting on a Hilbert space H").
inverse(r: ratio) -> ratio { \ }

# cents — logarithmic interval measurement.
#
# The standard psychoacoustic measurement scale. One octave =
# 1200 cents; one semitone in 12-TET = 100 cents; trained listeners
# resolve ~5 cents.
#
# Definition: cents(r) = 1200 * log₂(numerator / denominator).
#
# Useful examples (canonical values for cross-checking the lift):
#   1:1     0      cents  (unison; λ₀)
#   2:1   1200      cents  (octave; the doubling)
#   3:2    701.955  cents  (perfect fifth; the eigenvector)
#   4:3    498.045  cents  (perfect fourth; inverse of the fifth)
#   5:4    386.314  cents  (major third)
#   9:8    203.910  cents  (whole tone; comma carrier in the scale)
#   pythagorean_comma  23.460 cents (the closure residual of
#                                    twelve 3:2 fifths vs seven 2:1
#                                    octaves)
#
# Returns `ref` — the substrate's float-valued reference floor, per
# `glass.mirror`'s `weight: f64` precedent in opacity. The log₂ body
# is realisation-layer; the obligation block holds the substrate
# altitude until a consumer pulls.
cents(r: ratio) -> ref { \ }

# is_consonant — small-integer-ratio consonance verdict.
#
# Returns `pass` when the ratio's numerator AND denominator are small
# enough that the ratio resolves on the harmonic series within the
# substrate's spectral budget. Returns `partial(confidence)` for the
# graded consonances (mediant intervals; the borderline cases the
# dissonance curve resolves continuously). Returns
# `failure(reason)` when the ratio cannot consonate at the substrate's
# resolution (the irrational temperament-quotient ratios; the
# ratio whose terms exceed u32).
#
# The threshold is realisation-layer; the substrate declares the
# verdict-returning shape. `verdict` comes from `@glass` per the
# substrate floor (`shards/glass.mirror`).
#
# Spectrally: a consonance is an eigenvector of D with eigenvalue
# small in the holonomy norm — a direction in H that closes its loop.
# `is_consonant` reads the spectral-triple verdict at the audible
# register.
is_consonant(r: ratio) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/math/music/harmonic
out ratio
out pythagorean_comma
out comma_as_holonomy
out compose
out inverse
out cents
out is_consonant
